{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.8,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R2"],
      "pins": ["R2.1", "R2.2", "Q2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "Net-(Q2-G)"],
      "observed": "On the SkylabModule sheet, the gate pull-up resistor R2 on the Q2 (NTR2101P) gate node is drawn with value '10M' (10 MΩ), tied between +3V3 and Q2 pin 1 (gate).",
      "expected": "The specification states R2 is a 10 kΩ gate pull-up that keeps Q2's gate high (off) by default; a 10 kΩ value is required here, not 10 MΩ (three orders of magnitude too large).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "SkylabModule.kicad_sch: R2, value '10M', connected between +3V3 and Q2.1 (gate)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the gate pull-up R2 (10 kΩ, pulling Q2's gate high/off by default)"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 10 MΩ pull-up is far too weak to hold the P-channel MOSFET gate at source potential against leakage and noise. Q2 (the EPD high-side power switch) may not stay reliably off, can partially turn on, and the gate node becomes noise-sensitive — degrading the Display_Power_Switch rail control and aggravating the documented 'heats up while off' behaviour.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing otherwise matches the specification's connectivity, but R2 — the Q2 gate pull-up that the spec defines as 10 kΩ — is drawn as 10 MΩ, a three-orders-of-magnitude error that compromises the EPD power-switch off state; this is the one supported anomaly."
}

